<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isaías Medina Angarita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1897">1897</a>–<a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isaías <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> Angarita was a Venezuelan army officer who served as president from 1941 to 1945. Chosen as successor by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleazar-lopez-contreras">Eleazar López Contreras</a>, he legalised political parties, allowed greater press freedom and passed the Hydrocarbons Law of 1943, which raised the state's share of oil revenue. He was overthrown in October 1945 by a coup of young officers allied with Democratic Action, which opened the Trienio.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isaias-medina-angarita.jpg" alt="Isaías Medina Angarita" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_de_Isa%C3%ADas_Medina_Angarita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
